# Mosquitto ACL - copy to `aclfile` and extend per gateway.
#
# Principle: a gateway may publish ONLY under its own namespace and subscribe
# ONLY to its own command topic. It can neither read another site's telemetry
# nor forge readings for another device.

# --- backend ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The only identity allowed across the whole namespace.
user veritek-backend
topic readwrite technode/#

# --- one block per gateway -------------------------------------------------
# Username = the gateway uid; password = the token from
#   POST /api/admin/gateways/:id/token
# (stored only as a scrypt hash on our side).
#
# Copy this block for each unit, replacing GW-UID.

# user GW-UID
# topic write technode/GW-UID/telemetry
# topic write technode/GW-UID/status
# topic read  technode/GW-UID/command
# topic write technode/GW-UID/command/response

# Example, once the real device id is known:
# user TN-8623600786286128
# topic write technode/TN-8623600786286128/#
# topic read  technode/TN-8623600786286128/command

# No `pattern` or `topic` rule outside a user block: an unmatched client gets
# nothing, which is the behaviour we want.
